{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout.md; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md; cat pose-mcp/internal/pose/index_federated_material.go'","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-14\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates: spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit@defect-fix\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:index-material-does-not-ask-closeout\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nImpedir que o material de entrada do índice dependa do estado de fechamento: sob a política de revisão do fechamento adotada, `pose check` e toda operação que lê o índice sob um pin de geração travavam esperando por si mesmos.\n\n### Business value\nEm 2026-11-14 o harne8 adotou `closeout-review-policy` com `when-justified`, e o `pose check --tolerant` do hook de pre-commit ficou quase seis horas parado em `futex_wait`, com 49 s de CPU. O dump das goroutines mostrou o ciclo: a verificação das entradas do índice (`checkIndexInputs`) calcula o material federado (`BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn` → `FederatedRoadmapAcceptance`); sob a política adotada, uma aresta local de milestone ou roadmap pergunta à projeção terminal (`localScopeClosed`, introduzida pela spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, rodada 6, N22); a projeção lê o índice (`ReadIndex` → `checkIndexInputs`), que espera pela verificação em curso. Toda instância que adotar a política e tiver uma aresta local trava commits, checks e revisões.\n\n### Constraints\n- O gate de fechamento continua exigindo o fechamento das arestas locais; só o material de entrada do índice deixa de perguntar.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Não mudar a aceitação fora do cálculo do material do índice.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: When the engine computes an index's federated input material, it shall judge local milestone and roadmap edges by their source identity and status only, never by the terminal closeout projection, which is derived from the index being checked.\n- R2: Outside that computation, a local aggregate edge shall keep requiring the edge's scope closed under an adopted closeout review policy.\n- R3: Under an adopted closeout review policy with a local `after:` edge, the closeout state of a done spec read inside a scoped review operation with a pinned index generation shall finish.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança.\n\n### Compatibility\n- O material federado de uma instância sem a política adotada não muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/index_federated_material.go`: o store do material marca o cálculo.\n- `pose/federated_acceptance.go` e `pose/closeout_review_policy.go`: a pergunta à projeção terminal é pulada nesse cálculo.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/index_federated_material.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy_test.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:index-material-does-not-ask-closeout module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por `pose check` e pelos hooks, que leem o índice sob um pin de geração. Check permanente `index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestIndexMaterialDoesNotAskTheCloseoutOfALocalEdge|TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundSix$' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Nenhum novo: o material deixa de carregar um bloqueio de fechamento que o gate avalia de qualquer modo.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Marcar o cálculo do material e pular a projeção terminal nele (R1).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste de regressão do ciclo (R3) e o da aresta local sob a política (R2).\n- [x] Reproduzir no harne8 antes e depois.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-14\n- Context: o material de entrada do índice consultava estado derivado do próprio índice.\n- Options considered: (a) tornar a verificação de entradas reentrante (devolver desconhecido a quem pergunta de dentro dela); (b) o material não pergunta o estado de fechamento.\n- Decision: (b).\n- Rationale: (a) troca o travamento por um desconhecido permanente sob a política; (b) remove a dependência circular, e o material passa a ser só função dos artefatos de origem, como deve ser uma entrada.\n- Consequences: o bloqueio de uma aresta local ainda não fechada aparece no gate de fechamento, não no material do índice.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTeste da propriedade que quebra o ciclo: no cálculo do material, a aceitação de uma aresta local sob a política adotada não lê recibo de fechamento nem acusa o fechamento, e fora dele continua acusando (RoundSix); reprodução de ponta a ponta no harne8 antes e depois. Um fixture de CLI com a geração do índice vinculando material federado não reproduziu o ciclo, porque o fixture não monta esse vínculo como o harne8.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-14\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26; harne8 com a política adotada e o gitlink em 5e143371.\n- Notes: dump de goroutines do `pose check --tolerant` travado: 16 goroutines em `chan receive` em `checkIndexInputs`, com a pilha `checkIndexInputs` → `indexInputBinding` → `BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn` → `FederatedRoadmapAcceptance` → `localScopeClosed` → `closedByReceipt` → `getCloseoutState` → `ReviewCheck` → `ReadIndex` → `checkIndexInputs`. Com o binário corrigido, o mesmo `pose check --tolerant` do harne8, com a política adotada e as raízes que `scripts/pose-cli-local.sh` injeta, terminou em 71 s com sucesso, sem goroutine bloqueada; com o binário anterior, travava.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: o teste da propriedade reprova sem a correção e passa com ela; o `pose check` do harne8 sob a política adotada termina.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestIndexMaterialDoesNotAskTheCloseoutOfALocalEdge\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundSix\n- R3 [satisfied] check:index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration (reprodução no harne8 no log de execução)\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nO cálculo do material federado de entrada do índice julga arestas locais de milestone e roadmap pela identidade e pelo status da origem, sem perguntar o estado de fechamento; fora dele, nada muda.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- `pose/spec.go`, `pose/index_federated_material.go`, `pose/federated_acceptance.go`, `pose/closeout_review_policy.go`, teste novo, matriz.\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`; `pose check --tolerant` no harne8 com a política adotada.\n- Result: verde; o check termina em 71 s.\n\n### Residual risks\n- Outra leitura de estado derivado do índice dentro do cálculo do material reabriria o ciclo; o teste de regressão cobre o caminho conhecido.\n\n### Follow-ups\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\npackage pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io/fs\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// IndexFederatedSpecMaterial is the dependency-resolution projection emitted\n// for one spec by `pose index`.\ntype IndexFederatedSpecMaterial struct {\n\tSlug                  string               `json:\"slug\"`\n\tDependencyResolutions []ArtifactResolution `json:\"dependency_resolutions\"`\n}\n\n// IndexFederatedRoadmapMaterial is the acceptance projection emitted for one\n// roadmap by `pose index`.\ntype IndexFederatedRoadmapMaterial struct {\n\tSlug       string                           `json:\"slug\"`\n\tAcceptance FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport `json:\"acceptance\"`\n}\n\n// IndexFederatedMaterialProjection contains only the federated semantic\n// inputs represented in the generated indexes. It deliberately excludes\n// unrelated foreign files and roots.\ntype IndexFederatedMaterialProjection struct {\n\tSchemaVersion int                             `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tSpecs         []IndexFederatedSpecMaterial    `json:\"specs\"`\n\tRoadmaps      []IndexFederatedRoadmapMaterial `json:\"roadmaps\"`\n}\n\n// IndexFederatedMaterial carries both the semantic input projection and the\n// source records used to build index outputs. The projection is shared by the\n// builder and the generation binding so output bytes and their binding cannot\n// be computed from separate, interleaved reads.\ntype IndexFederatedMaterial struct {\n\tProjection                IndexFederatedMaterialProjection\n\tSpecs                     []Spec\n\tRoadmaps                  []Roadmap\n\tSpecDependencyResolutions map[string][]ArtifactResolution\n\tRoadmapAcceptances        map[string]FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport\n\tProjects                  []string\n\tReferencedProjects        []string\n\tRequiresPrimaryRevision   bool\n}\n\n// BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn returns the specs, roadmaps, semantic\n// projections and exact foreign projects whose contents were resolved. The\n// Store must carry the operation's authorized resolver when one has already\n// been established; it is reused unchanged except for the captured Files the\n// operation view supplies.\nfunc BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn(store Store) (IndexFederatedMaterial, error) {\n\tstore.indexMaterial = true\n\tresolver := ArtifactResolver{}\n\tproject := store.FederatedProjectID\n\tif store.FederatedResolver != nil {\n\t\tresolver = *store.FederatedResolver\n\t\tif resolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: authorized project roots are unavailable for index material\")\n\t\t}\n\t} else {\n\t\tvar err error\n\t\tresolver, project, err = EnvironmentArtifactResolverIn(store.fsys(), store.Root, \"\")\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: index material resolver: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif project == \"\" {\n\t\tvar found, ambiguous, overflow bool\n\t\tproject, found, ambiguous, overflow = uniqueProjectIDForRootIn(store.fsys(), resolver.Roots, store.Root, resolver.Authorize)\n\t\tif overflow {\n\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: index material root identity exceeds the authorized-root snapshot budget\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif ambiguous {\n\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: index material root has multiple authorized project identities\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tproject = DefaultProjectIDIn(store.fsys(), store.Root)\n\t\t\tif ValidateSlug(project) != nil || resolver.Authorize != nil && !resolver.Authorize(project) {\n\t\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: index material project identity is not authorized\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbound, err := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(project)\n\t\t\tif err != nil || !sameProjectRoot(store.fsys(), bound.Root, store.Root) {\n\t\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: index material root is outside the authorized project registry\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif ValidateSlug(project) != nil {\n\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, errors.New(\"pose: index material project identity is unavailable\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Fresh for this build, never inherited from an earlier advisory operation.\n\tresolver = resolver.WithSpecSnapshots()\n\tspecs, err := store.ListSpecs(\"\", \"\")\n\tif err != nil && !errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: listing specs for index material: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\troadmaps, err := store.ListRoadmaps()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: listing roadmaps for index material: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(specs, func(i, j int) bool { return specs[i].Slug < specs[j].Slug })\n\tsort.Slice(roadmaps, func(i, j int) bool { return roadmaps[i].Slug < roadmaps[j].Slug })\n\n\tmaterial := IndexFederatedMaterial{\n\t\tSpecs:                     specs,\n\t\tRoadmaps:                  roadmaps,\n\t\tSpecDependencyResolutions: make(map[string][]ArtifactResolution, len(specs)),\n\t\tRoadmapAcceptances:        make(map[string]FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, len(roadmaps)),\n\t\tProjection: IndexFederatedMaterialProjection{\n\t\t\tSchemaVersion: 1,\n\t\t\tSpecs:         make([]IndexFederatedSpecMaterial, 0, len(specs)),\n\t\t\tRoadmaps:      make([]IndexFederatedRoadmapMaterial, 0, len(roadmaps)),\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\tprojects := map[string]bool{}\n\treferencedProjects := map[string]bool{}\n\taddProject := func(id string) {\n\t\tif id == \"\" || id == project {\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\treferencedProjects[id] = true\n\t\tif resolver.Authorize != nil && !resolver.Authorize(id) {\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, err := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(id); err == nil {\n\t\t\t// Include only foreign roots named by this semantic projection. A\n\t\t\t// project discovered for reading still has to pass the explicit-root\n\t\t\t// write guard before this generation can be published.\n\t\t\tprojects[id] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, spec := range specs {\n\t\tresolutions := make([]ArtifactResolution, 0, len(spec.DependsOn))\n\t\tsemanticResolutions := make([]ArtifactResolution, 0, len(spec.DependsOn))\n\t\tfor _, raw := range spec.DependsOn {\n\t\t\tresolution := resolver.Resolve(project, raw)\n\t\t\tresolutions = append(resolutions, resolution)\n\t\t\tsemanticResolution := resolution\n\t\t\t// Same-project resolution revisions describe repository HEAD, while\n\t\t\t// the identity, state, status, digest and dependency edges below carry\n\t\t\t// the semantic result. Keep local unrelated commits out of the index\n\t\t\t// binding; the generated output still preserves the observed revision.\n\t\t\tif semanticResolution.Identity.Project == project {\n\t\t\t\tsemanticResolution.Revision = \"\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsemanticResolutions = append(semanticResolutions, semanticResolution)\n\t\t\taddProject(resolution.Identity.Project)\n\t\t}\n\t\tmaterial.SpecDependencyResolutions[spec.Slug] = resolutions\n\t\tmaterial.Projection.Specs = append(material.Projection.Specs, IndexFederatedSpecMaterial{\n\t\t\tSlug: spec.Slug, DependencyResolutions: semanticResolutions,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tfor _, roadmap := range roadmaps {\n\t\tacceptance, err := store.FederatedRoadmapAcceptance(project, roadmap.Slug, resolver)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn IndexFederatedMaterial{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated roadmap %s: %w\", roadmap.Slug, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tmaterial.RoadmapAcceptances[roadmap.Slug] = acceptance\n\t\tmaterial.Projection.Roadmaps = append(material.Projection.Roadmaps, IndexFederatedRoadmapMaterial{\n\t\t\tSlug: roadmap.Slug, Acceptance: indexSemanticAcceptanceReport(project, acceptance),\n\t\t})\n\t\tfor _, dependency := range acceptance.Manifest.Dependencies {\n\t\t\taddProject(dependency.Identity.Project)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tmaterial.Projects = make([]string, 0, len(projects))\n\tfor id := range projects {\n\t\tmaterial.Projects = append(material.Projects, id)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(material.Projects)\n\tmaterial.ReferencedProjects = make([]string, 0, len(referencedProjects))\n\tfor id := range referencedProjects {\n\t\tmaterial.ReferencedProjects = append(material.ReferencedProjects, id)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(material.ReferencedProjects)\n\tmaterial.RequiresPrimaryRevision = indexMaterialRequiresPrimaryRevision(store, resolver, project, material)\n\treturn material, nil\n}\n\nfunc indexMaterialRequiresPrimaryRevision(store Store, resolver ArtifactResolver, localProject string, material IndexFederatedMaterial) bool {\n\tfiles := store.fsys()\n\tfor _, report := range material.RoadmapAcceptances {\n\t\tfor _, dependency := range report.Manifest.Dependencies {\n\t\t\tif dependency.Identity.Project == localProject && dependency.SourceDigest != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t// Roadmap acceptance proves the local artifact against its\n\t\t\t\t// committed revision; a worktree-only answer is not enough.\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif dependency.Identity.Project == \"\" || dependency.Identity.Project == localProject || dependency.SourceDigest == \"\" || dependency.SourceRevision == \"\" || !hasGitMetadataIn(files, store.Root) {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tforeign, err := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(dependency.Identity.Project)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tlocalReal, localErr := files.EvalSymlinks(store.Root)\n\t\t\tforeignReal, foreignErr := files.EvalSymlinks(foreign.Root)\n\t\t\tif localErr != nil || foreignErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trelative, err := filepath.Rel(localReal, foreignReal)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tinside := relative == \".\" || relative != \"..\" && !strings.HasPrefix(relative, \"..\"+string(filepath.Separator))\n\t\t\tif inside {\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// indexSemanticAcceptanceReport drops only local repository revisions whose\n// changes do not alter the accepted artifact projection. This normalized copy\n// is used only for the input binding; generated output keeps the exact report\n// produced by the federated acceptance operation. The acceptance code already\n// uses artifact-level resolution and trust digests for meaningful local and\n// foreign changes, so recompute the binding copy's digest after normalization.\nfunc indexSemanticAcceptanceReport(localProject string, report FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport) FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport {\n\treport.Manifest.Dependencies = append([]FederatedDependency(nil), report.Manifest.Dependencies...)\n\treport.Manifest.CoordinatorRevision = \"\"\n\tfor i := range report.Manifest.Dependencies {\n\t\tif report.Manifest.Dependencies[i].Identity.Project == localProject {\n\t\t\treport.Manifest.Dependencies[i].SourceRevision = \"\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treport.Manifest.Digest = \"\"\n\treport.Manifest.Digest = canonicalFederatedDigest(report.Manifest)\n\treturn report\n}\n\n// IndexFederatedMaterialDigest returns the stable semantic digest bound to an\n// index generation. The digest does not include root paths or unrelated files.\nfunc IndexFederatedMaterialDigest(material IndexFederatedMaterialProjection) (string, bool) {\n\traw, err := json.Marshal(material)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:]), true\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,540p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go; sed -n '220,380p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go; rg -n 'BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn|indexMaterial|AggregateDependencyClosed' pose-mcp/internal/pose; rg -n 'index-material|closeout-review-policy' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,540p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go; sed -n '220,380p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go; rg -n 'BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn|indexMaterial|AggregateDependencyClosed' pose-mcp/internal/pose; rg -n 'index-material|closeout-review-policy' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"package pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\nconst FederatedRoadmapPolicySchemaVersion = 1\n\nconst (\n\tmaxFederatedPolicyBytes          = 256 << 10\n\tmaxFederatedGovernanceInputBytes = 2 << 20\n)\n\ntype FederatedProjectTrust struct {\n\tContractDigest string `json:\"contract_digest\"`\n\tPolicyDigest   string `json:\"policy_digest\"`\n\tRevision       string `json:\"revision\"`\n}\n\ntype FederatedRoadmapPolicy struct {\n\tSchemaVersion   int                              `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tEnabled         bool                             `json:\"enabled\"`\n\tAdoptedAt       string                           `json:\"adopted_at,omitempty\"`\n\tTrustedProjects map[string]FederatedProjectTrust `json:\"trusted_projects,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype FederatedDependencyEvidence struct {\n\tID                 string `json:\"id\"`\n\tCheck              string `json:\"check\"`\n\tEvidenceClass      string `json:\"evidence_class\"`\n\tSubjectObservation string `json:\"subject_observation\"`\n}\n\ntype FederatedDependency struct {\n\tRef                  string                        `json:\"ref\"`\n\tRelationship         string                        `json:\"relationship\"`\n\tRelationships        []string                      `json:\"relationships,omitempty\"`\n\tIdentity             ArtifactRef                   `json:\"identity\"`\n\tResolutionState      string                        `json:\"resolution_state\"`\n\tStatus               string                        `json:\"status,omitempty\"`\n\tSourceRevision       string                        `json:\"source_revision,omitempty\"`\n\tSourceDigest         string                        `json:\"source_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tSourceContractDigest string                        `json:\"source_contract_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tSourcePolicyDigest   string                        `json:\"source_policy_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tReviewBundleID       string                        `json:\"review_bundle_id,omitempty\"`\n\tReviewBundleDigest   string                        `json:\"review_bundle_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tImplementationDigest string                        `json:\"implementation_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tPlanDigest           string                        `json:\"plan_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tGoverningContracts   []string                      `json:\"governing_contracts,omitempty\"`\n\tEvidence             []FederatedDependencyEvidence `json:\"evidence,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype FederatedRoadmapManifest struct {\n\tSchemaVersion       int                   `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tCoordinator         ArtifactRef           `json:\"coordinator\"`\n\tCoordinatorRevision string                `json:\"coordinator_revision,omitempty\"`\n\tTrustPolicyDigest   string                `json:\"trust_policy_digest,omitempty\"`\n\tDependencies        []FederatedDependency `json:\"dependencies\"`\n\tReady               bool                  `json:\"ready\"`\n\tBlockers            []string              `json:\"blockers\"`\n\tDigest              string                `json:\"digest\"`\n}\n\ntype FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport struct {\n\tManifest FederatedRoadmapManifest `json:\"manifest\"`\n\tReady    bool                     `json:\"ready\"`\n\tBlockers []string                 `json:\"blockers\"`\n}\n\ntype federatedRoadmapEdge struct {\n\tproject      string\n\traw          string\n\trelationship string\n}\n\ntype federatedQueuedRef struct {\n\tproject      string\n\tparent       string\n\traw          string\n\trelationship string\n}\n\n// FederatedProjectTrustFor computes the exact governance inputs a consumer\n// must accept for one source project. It is read-only: callers still have to\n// record the returned digests in their own policy.\nfunc FederatedProjectTrustForIn(files Files, root, projectID string) (FederatedProjectTrust, error) {\n\tif ValidateSlug(projectID) != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedProjectTrust{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid federated project id\")\n\t}\n\trevision := gitHeadAtRootIn(files, root, federatedAcceptanceProducer)\n\tif !isGitRevision(revision) {\n\t\treturn FederatedProjectTrust{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated-project-revision-unavailable\")\n\t}\n\tcontractFiles := []string{\".pose/schema-version\", \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\"}\n\tpolicyFiles := []string{\".pose/policy/artifacts.json\", \".pose/policy/delivery.json\", \".pose/policy/review.json\"}\n\tcontracts, err := committedFederatedInputs(files, root, contractFiles)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedProjectTrust{}, err\n\t}\n\tpolicies, err := committedFederatedInputs(files, root, policyFiles)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedProjectTrust{}, err\n\t}\n\treturn FederatedProjectTrust{ContractDigest: canonicalFederatedDigest(contracts), PolicyDigest: canonicalFederatedDigest(policies), Revision: revision}, nil\n}\n\n// FederatedProjectTrustFor reads and writes the filesystem directly; FederatedProjectTrustForIn takes the\n// operation's files.\nfunc FederatedProjectTrustFor(root, projectID string) (FederatedProjectTrust, error) {\n\treturn FederatedProjectTrustForIn(NativeFiles(), root, projectID)\n}\n\nfunc LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicyIn(files Files, root string) (FederatedRoadmapPolicy, string, error) {\n\trel := \".pose/policy/federation.json\"\n\tif err := ValidateArtifactPathIn(files, root, rel, false); err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federation-policy-path\")\n\t}\n\tpath := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(rel))\n\tinfo, err := files.Stat(path)\n\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federation-policy-unavailable\")\n\t}\n\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federation-policy-unavailable\")\n\t}\n\tfile, err := files.Open(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federation-policy-unavailable\")\n\t}\n\traw, readErr := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(file, maxFederatedPolicyBytes+1))\n\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n\tif readErr != nil || closeErr != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federation-policy-unavailable\")\n\t}\n\tif len(raw) > maxFederatedPolicyBytes {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federation-policy-too-large\")\n\t}\n\tvar policy FederatedRoadmapPolicy\n\tif rejectDuplicateJSONKeysAndControls(raw) != nil || strictJSONBytes(raw, &policy) != nil || policy.SchemaVersion != FederatedRoadmapPolicySchemaVersion {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: unsupported-federation-contract\")\n\t}\n\tif policy.Enabled {\n\t\tif _, err := time.Parse(time.DateOnly, policy.AdoptedAt); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federation-adoption-date\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor projectID, pin := range policy.TrustedProjects {\n\t\tif ValidateSlug(projectID) != nil || !isSHA256(pin.ContractDigest) || !isSHA256(pin.PolicyDigest) || !isGitRevision(pin.Revision) {\n\t\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapPolicy{}, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-project-trust\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn policy, digestBytes(raw), nil\n}\n\n// LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicy reads and writes the filesystem directly; LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicyIn takes the\n// operation's files.\nfunc LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicy(root string) (FederatedRoadmapPolicy, string, error) {\n\treturn LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicyIn(NativeFiles(), root)\n}\n\nfunc strictJSONBytes(raw []byte, target any) error {\n\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n\tdecoder.DisallowUnknownFields()\n\tif err := decoder.Decode(target); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tvar extra any\n\tif err := decoder.Decode(&extra); err != io.EOF {\n\t\tif err == nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"trailing JSON content\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc isSHA256(value string) bool {\n\tif !strings.HasPrefix(value, \"sha256:\") || len(value) != len(\"sha256:\")+64 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\t_, err := hex.DecodeString(strings.TrimPrefix(value, \"sha256:\"))\n\treturn err == nil\n}\n\nfunc isGitRevision(value string) bool {\n\tif len(value) != 40 && len(value) != 64 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\t_, err := hex.DecodeString(value)\n\treturn err == nil\n}\n\nfunc committedFederatedInputs(files Files, root string, paths []string) (map[string]string, error) {\n\tinputs := make(map[string]string, len(paths))\n\tfor _, rel := range paths {\n\t\tif err := ValidateArtifactPathIn(files, root, rel, false); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tabsolute := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(rel))\n\t\tinfo, err := files.Stat(absolute)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: missing-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() || info.Size() > maxFederatedGovernanceInputBytes {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !artifactPathWithin(files, root, absolute) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tfile, err := files.Open(absolute)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: missing-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tworking, readErr := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(file, maxFederatedGovernanceInputBytes+1))\n\t\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n\t\tif readErr != nil || closeErr != nil || len(working) > maxFederatedGovernanceInputBytes {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\ttop, err := captureFederatedGit(files, root, \"rev-parse\", \"--show-toplevel\")\n\t\tif err != nil || !sameProjectRoot(files, root, strings.TrimSpace(string(top))) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated-project-revision-unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\trevision, err := captureFederatedGit(files, root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"HEAD\")\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated-project-revision-unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tobject := strings.TrimSpace(string(revision)) + \":\" + filepath.ToSlash(rel)\n\t\tblobSize, err := captureFederatedGit(files, root, \"cat-file\", \"-s\", object)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated-project-revision-unavailable\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tvar committedSize int64\n\t\tif _, err := fmt.Sscan(strings.TrimSpace(string(blobSize)), &committedSize); err != nil || committedSize < 0 || committedSize > maxFederatedGovernanceInputBytes {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid-federated-governance-input\")\n\t\t}\n\t\thead, err := captureFederatedGit(files, root, \"show\", object)\n\t\tif err != nil || !bytes.Equal(working, head) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: federated-governance-input-not-committed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tinputs[rel] = digestBytes(working)\n\t}\n\treturn inputs, nil\n}\n\nfunc canonicalFederatedDigest(value any) string {\n\traw, _ := json.Marshal(value)\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) FederatedRoadmapAcceptance(projectID, slug string, resolver ArtifactResolver) (FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, error) {\n\trm, err := s.GetRoadmap(slug)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, err\n\t}\n\tif resolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: project roots are unavailable\")\n\t}\n\treturn s.federatedAcceptance(projectID, ArtifactRef{Project: projectID, Kind: \"roadmap\", Slug: slug}, collectFederatedRoadmapEdges(projectID, rm), resolver)\n}\n\n// FederatedMilestoneAcceptance restricts roadmap acceptance to one milestone:\n// the roadmap's consumed outcomes, plus that milestone's predecessors, member\n// specs and consumed outcomes. Members of a later milestone do not gate an\n// earlier one, matching local milestone closeout, and the depends_on of the\n// roadmap binds the close of the roadmap alone (ADR\n// a-milestone-answers-to-its-own-edges).\nfunc (s Store) FederatedMilestoneAcceptance(projectID, slug, milestone string, resolver ArtifactResolver) (FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, error) {\n\treturn s.milestoneAcceptance(projectID, slug, milestone, resolver, false)\n}\n\n// milestoneAcceptance builds the acceptance of one milestone. roadmapDependencies\n// keeps the depends_on of the roadmap, which is how a bundle sealed before that\n// edge moved to the roadmap reads.\nfunc (s Store) milestoneAcceptance(projectID, slug, milestone string, resolver ArtifactResolver, roadmapDependencies bool) (FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, error) {\n\trm, err := s.GetRoadmap(slug)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, err\n\t}\n\tif resolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: project roots are unavailable\")\n\t}\n\tselected := *rm\n\tselected.Milestones = nil\n\tif !roadmapDependencies {\n\t\tselected.DependsOn = nil\n\t}\n\tfor _, candidate := range rm.Milestones {\n\t\tif candidate.ID == milestone {\n\t\t\tselected.Milestones = append(selected.Milestones, candidate)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(selected.Milestones) == 0 {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: milestone %s not found in roadmap %s\", milestone, slug)\n\t}\n\tcoordinator := ArtifactRef{Project: projectID, Kind: \"milestone\", Slug: slug, Milestone: milestone}\n\treturn s.federatedAcceptance(projectID, coordinator, collectFederatedRoadmapEdges(projectID, &selected), resolver)\n}\n\n// FederatedSpecAcceptance applies roadmap acceptance to the external\n// dependencies of one spec. It reports applies=false for a spec whose\n// depends_on names no other project, so its review and closeout keep their\n// previous contract. Local dependencies stay governed by lifecycle checks.\nfunc (s Store) FederatedSpecAcceptance(projectID, slug string, resolver ArtifactResolver) (FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, bool, error) {\n\tsp, err := s.GetSpec(slug)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, false, err\n\t}\n\tedges := []federatedRoadmapEdge{}\n\tfor _, raw := range sp.DependsOn {\n\t\tref, err := ParseArtifactRef(raw)\n\t\tif err != nil || ref.Project == \"\" || ref.Project == projectID {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tedges = append(edges, federatedRoadmapEdge{project: projectID, raw: raw, relationship: \"prerequisite\"})\n\t}\n\tif len(edges) == 0 {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tcoordinator := ArtifactRef{Project: projectID, Kind: \"spec\", Slug: slug}\n\tif resolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\t// Fail closed without failing the command: a checkout with no roots\n\t\t// can still read the spec but can never close it.\n\t\treturn federatedBlockedReport(s.fsys(), s, coordinator, \"project-roots-unavailable\"), true, nil\n\t}\n\treport, err := s.federatedAcceptance(projectID, coordinator, edges, resolver)\n\treturn report, true, err\n}\n\nfunc federatedBlockedReport(files Files, s Store, coordinator ArtifactRef, blocker string) FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport {\n\tmanifest := FederatedRoadmapManifest{SchemaVersion: 1, Coordinator: coordinator, CoordinatorRevision: federatedArtifactLastChange(files, s, coordinator), Dependencies: []FederatedDependency{}, Blockers: []string{blocker}}\n\tmanifest.Digest = canonicalFederatedDigest(manifest)\n\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{Manifest: manifest, Blockers: []string{blocker}}\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) federatedAcceptance(projectID string, coordinator ArtifactRef, edges []federatedRoadmapEdge, resolver ArtifactResolver) (FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport, error) {\n\tpolicy, policyDigest, err := LoadFederatedRoadmapPolicyIn(s.fsys(), s.Root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{}, err\n\t}\n\trevision := gitHeadAtRootIn(s.fsys(), s.Root, federatedAcceptanceProducer)\n\tcoordinatorRevision := revision\n\tif stable := federatedArtifactLastChange(s.fsys(), s, coordinator); stable != \"\" {\n\t\tcoordinatorRevision = stable\n\t}\n\treport := FederatedRoadmapAcceptanceReport{Manifest: FederatedRoadmapManifest{\n\t\tSchemaVersion: 1, Coordinator: coordinator, CoordinatorRevision: coordinatorRevision,\n\t\tTrustPolicyDigest: policyDigest, Dependencies: []FederatedDependency{},\n\t}, Blockers: []string{}}\n\tqueue := []federatedQueuedRef{}\n\tfor _, edge := range edges {\n\t\tqueue = append(queue, federatedQueuedRef{project: edge.project, parent: edge.project, raw: edge.raw, relationship: edge.relationship})\n\t}\n\tvisited := map[string]bool{}\n\tdependencyIndexes := map[string]int{}\n\tprojectRoots := map[string]Store{projectID: s}\n\tsnapshotRevisions := map[string]string{}\n\tif revision != \"\" {\n\t\tsnapshotRevisions[projectID] = revision\n\t}\n\tfor len(queue) > 0 {\n\t\titem := queue[0]\n\t\tqueue = queue[1:]\n\t\tresolved := resolver.Resolve(item.project, item.raw)\n\t\tidentity := resolved.Identity\n\t\tif identity.Project == \"\" {\n\t\t\tidentity.Project = item.project\n\t\t}\n\t\tkey := identity.String()\n\t\tif visited[key] {\n\t\t\tif index, ok := dependencyIndexes[key]; ok {\n\t\t\t\tentry := &report.Manifest.Dependencies[index]\n\t\t\t\tfound := item.relationship == entry.Relationship\n\t\t\t\tfor _, relationship := range entry.Relationships {\n\t\t\t\t\tfound = found || relationship == item.relationship\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\t\t\tentry.Relationships = append(entry.Relationships, item.relationship)\n\t\t\t\t\tsort.Strings(entry.Relationships)\n\t\t\t\t\tentry.Relationship = entry.Relationships[0]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(visited) >= 256 {\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, \"resolution-limit\")\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tvisited[key] = true\n\t\tentry := FederatedDependency{Ref: key, Relationship: item.relationship, Relationships: []string{item.relationship}, Identity: identity, ResolutionState: resolved.State, Status: resolved.Status, SourceRevision: resolved.Revision, SourceDigest: resolved.Digest}\n\t\t// The dependency keeps the identity it was named by, as the manifest\n\t\t// records it; a transferred artifact is proven at its canonical\n\t\t// destination: its store, revision, trust and closeout (review\n\t\t// round 7, N25). The resolver authorized the redirect chain.\n\t\tproven := identity\n\t\tif resolved.CanonicalIdentity != nil {\n\t\t\tproven = *resolved.CanonicalIdentity\n\t\t}\n\t\tdependencyIndexes[key] = len(report.Manifest.Dependencies)\n\t\tif !resolved.Resolved {\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+resolved.State)\n\t\t\treport.Manifest.Dependencies = append(report.Manifest.Dependencies, entry)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif selected, exists := snapshotRevisions[proven.Project]; exists && selected != \"\" && resolved.Revision != selected {\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":source-revision-changed-during-resolution\")\n\t\t} else if _, exists := snapshotRevisions[proven.Project]; !exists && resolved.Revision != \"\" {\n\t\t\tsnapshotRevisions[proven.Project] = resolved.Revision\n\t\t}\n\t\tgraphValid := true\n\t\tif reason := resolver.ValidateGraph(item.project, item.raw); reason != \"\" {\n\t\t\tgraphValid = false\n\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = reason\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+reason)\n\t\t}\n\t\tstatusDone := resolved.Status == \"done\"\n\t\tif !statusDone {\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":not-done\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsource, sourceErr := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(proven.Project)\n\t\tif sourceErr != nil {\n\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = projectResolutionState(sourceErr)\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\treport.Manifest.Dependencies = append(report.Manifest.Dependencies, entry)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tsource = resolver.withSpecSnapshot(proven.Project, source)\n\t\tprojectRoots[proven.Project] = source\n\t\tsource.FederatedProjectID = proven.Project\n\t\tsource.FederatedResolver = &resolver\n\t\tartifactValid := true\n\t\tif err := verifyFederatedArtifactAtRevision(s.fsys(), source, proven, resolved); err != nil {\n\t\t\tartifactValid = false\n\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = err.Error()\n\t\t\tblocker := key + \":\" + err.Error()\n\t\t\tif err.Error() == federatedSourceUncommitted {\n\t\t\t\tblocker += \": commit the artifact, its working file differs from its revision\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, blocker)\n\t\t}\n\t\t// Same-project dependencies need the revision of their own artifact.\n\t\t// Using repository HEAD makes every unrelated evidence commit stale a\n\t\t// sealed milestone or roadmap. External dependencies retain the explicit\n\t\t// whole-repository pin checked below.\n\t\tif proven.Project == projectID {\n\t\t\tif stable := federatedArtifactLastChange(s.fsys(), source, proven); stable != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tentry.SourceRevision = stable\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t// Under an adopted closeout review policy a local milestone or\n\t\t\t// roadmap is closed by its explicit close, never by the status\n\t\t\t// its members give it: the edge asks the terminal projection,\n\t\t\t// along a chain that stops at a cycle (review round 6, N22).\n\t\t\tif statusDone && graphValid && !s.indexMaterial && (proven.Kind == \"milestone\" || proven.Kind == \"roadmap\") {\n\t\t\t\tif adopted, err := s.closeoutReviewPolicyAdopted(); err != nil || adopted && !s.localScopeClosed(localFederatedScope(proven)) {\n\t\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":closeout-not-terminal\")\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif proven.Project != projectID {\n\t\t\t// Do not recurse into source closeout when graph traversal has already\n\t\t\t// found a cycle or stale artifact. The blocker is conclusive, and\n\t\t\t// recursively asking each side of a cycle for its review would never\n\t\t\t// converge.\n\t\t\tgitlinkValid := true\n\t\t\tpin, pinErr := FederatedProjectTrustForIn(s.fsys(), source.Root, proven.Project)\n\t\t\tif pinErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = pinErr.Error()\n\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tentry.SourceContractDigest, entry.SourcePolicyDigest = pin.ContractDigest, pin.PolicyDigest\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !policy.Enabled {\n\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = \"consumer-trust-not-adopted\"\n\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\taccepted, exists := policy.TrustedProjects[proven.Project]\n\t\t\t\tif pinErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\t// The pin error was recorded above; retain the stable state.\n\t\t\t\t} else if !exists {\n\t\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = \"consumer-trust-not-adopted\"\n\t\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\t\t} else if accepted != pin {\n\t\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = \"consumer-trust-stale\"\n\t\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tif proven.Project == item.parent {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// This edge remains inside the selected source repository;\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// its local artifacts inherit that repository's pin.\n\t\t\t\t\t} else if parentStore, parentErr := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(item.parent); parentErr != nil || !federatedGitlinkMatchesIn(s.fsys(), parentStore, source, resolved.Revision) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tgitlinkValid = false\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif parentErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = projectResolutionState(parentErr)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = \"gitlink-revision-mismatch\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, key+\":\"+entry.ResolutionState)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\taccepted, trusted := policy.TrustedProjects[proven.Project]\n\t\t\tproofInputsReady := graphValid && statusDone && artifactValid && pinErr == nil && policy.Enabled && trusted && accepted == pin && gitlinkValid\n\t\t\tif proofInputsReady {\n\t\t\t\tbundleID, bundleDigest, subjectDigest, planDigest, contracts, evidence, proofBlockers := federatedSourceProof(s.fsys(), source, proven, resolved.Revision)\n\t\t\t\tentry.ReviewBundleID, entry.ReviewBundleDigest = bundleID, bundleDigest\n\t\t\t\tentry.ImplementationDigest, entry.PlanDigest = subjectDigest, planDigest\n\t\t\t\tentry.GoverningContracts, entry.Evidence = contracts, evidence\n\t\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, proofBlockers...)\n\t\t\t\tif len(proofBlockers) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\tentry.ResolutionState = \"source-evidence-incomplete\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treport.Manifest.Dependencies = append(report.Manifest.Dependencies, entry)\n\t\tfor _, dep := range resolved.Dependencies {\n\t\t\tqueue = append(queue, federatedQueuedRef{project: dep.Project, parent: proven.Project, raw: dep.String(), relationship: \"prerequisite\"})\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor project, selected := range snapshotRevisions {\n\t\tif selected == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\troot, ok := projectRoots[project]\n\t\tif ok && gitHeadAtRootIn(s.fsys(), root.Root, federatedAcceptanceProducer) != selected {\n\t\t\treport.Blockers = append(report.Blockers, \"source-snapshot-changed-during-resolution:\"+project)\n\t\t}\n\t\tidentity, diagnostic := s.closeoutCanonicalMember(strings.TrimSpace(raw), project)\n\t\tif diagnostic != \"\" {\n\t\t\tdiagnostics = append(diagnostics, diagnostic)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !seen[identity] {\n\t\t\tseen[identity] = true\n\t\t\tmembers = append(members, identity)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(members)\n\treturn members, diagnostics\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) closeoutCanonicalMember(raw, project string) (string, string) {\n\tref, err := ParseArtifactRef(raw)\n\tif err != nil || ref.Kind != \"spec\" || ref.Milestone != \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Sprintf(\"member %q is not a spec reference\", raw)\n\t}\n\tif ref.Project == \"\" {\n\t\tref.Project = project\n\t}\n\tresolve := func(why string) (string, string) {\n\t\tif s.FederatedResolver == nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Sprintf(\"member %s %s and no federated resolver is bound to follow it\", ref.String(), why)\n\t\t}\n\t\tresolved := s.FederatedResolver.Resolve(project, ref.String())\n\t\tif !resolved.Resolved {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Sprintf(\"member %s did not resolve: %s\", ref.String(), resolved.State)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif resolved.CanonicalIdentity != nil {\n\t\t\treturn resolved.CanonicalIdentity.String(), \"\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn resolved.Identity.String(), \"\"\n\t}\n\tif ref.Project != project {\n\t\treturn resolve(\"belongs to another project\")\n\t}\n\t_, found, err := readSpecTransferRedirect(s.fsys(), s, ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Sprintf(\"member %s has an unverifiable redirect: %v\", ref.String(), err)\n\t}\n\tif found {\n\t\t// The resolver follows the whole chain, with its cycle and depth\n\t\t// limits and the destination's authorization: the immediate\n\t\t// destination may itself have moved.\n\t\treturn resolve(\"was transferred\")\n\t}\n\tif _, err := s.GetSpec(ref.Slug); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Sprintf(\"member %s names no spec of this project\", ref.String())\n\t}\n\treturn ref.String(), \"\"\n}\n\n// CloseoutMemberTarget resolves a milestone member to the spec whose closeout\n// stands for it, as the closeout review policy counts it: a local member a\n// verified transfer moved is followed to its canonical destination, which is\n// local (its slug) or external (its identity, judged by federated\n// acceptance). A redirect that cannot be followed is reported, never read as\n// the redirect stub the transfer left behind (review round 6, N24).\nfunc (s Store) CloseoutMemberTarget(raw string) (string, bool, string) {\n\tslug, external := s.milestoneMember(raw)\n\tif external {\n\t\treturn slug, true, \"\"\n\t}\n\t// The project the store is bound to, as milestoneMember reads a\n\t// qualified member, else the one the root declares.\n\tproject := s.FederatedProjectID\n\tif project == \"\" {\n\t\tid, err := s.WriteProjectID()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, \"member \" + raw + \" cannot be resolved: \" + err.Error()\n\t\t}\n\t\tproject = id\n\t}\n\t_, found, err := readSpecTransferRedirect(s.fsys(), s, ArtifactRef{Project: project, Kind: \"spec\", Slug: slug})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, \"member \" + raw + \" has an unverifiable redirect: \" + err.Error()\n\t}\n\tif !found {\n\t\treturn slug, false, \"\"\n\t}\n\tif s.FederatedResolver == nil || s.FederatedResolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\tresolver, _, err := EnvironmentArtifactResolverIn(s.fsys(), s.Root, \"\")\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, \"member \" + raw + \" was transferred and no resolver can follow it: \" + err.Error()\n\t\t}\n\t\ts.FederatedResolver = &resolver\n\t}\n\tcanonical, diagnostic := s.closeoutCanonicalMember(strings.TrimSpace(raw), project)\n\tif diagnostic != \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, diagnostic\n\t}\n\tref, err := ParseArtifactRef(canonical)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, \"member \" + raw + \" resolved to \" + canonical + \", which is not a spec reference\"\n\t}\n\tif ref.Project == \"\" || ref.Project == project {\n\t\treturn ref.Slug, false, \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn canonical, true, \"\"\n}\n\n// AggregateDependencyClosed reports whether a resolved dependency on a\n// milestone or roadmap is closed, beyond the status its members give it:\n// under the closeout review policy its owning project adopted, only the\n// terminal projection closes it (an explicit close with its receipt, or a\n// verified closure from before adoption). A spec, or an aggregate scope of a\n// project still on the legacy rule, keeps its status contract. A transferred\n// artifact is judged at its canonical destination; a project whose store or\n// policy cannot be read is not proven closed (review round 7, N27).\nfunc (s Store) AggregateDependencyClosed(resolver ArtifactResolver, localProject string, resolved ArtifactResolution) (bool, string) {\n\tidentity := resolved.Identity\n\tif resolved.CanonicalIdentity != nil {\n\t\tidentity = *resolved.CanonicalIdentity\n\t}\n\tif identity.Kind != \"milestone\" && identity.Kind != \"roadmap\" || s.indexMaterial {\n\t\treturn true, \"\"\n\t}\n\tif identity.Project == \"\" {\n\t\tidentity.Project = localProject\n\t}\n\tscope := localFederatedScope(identity)\n\towner := s\n\tif identity.Project != localProject {\n\t\tif resolver.Roots == nil {\n\t\t\treturn false, scope + \" of \" + identity.Project + \" cannot be checked for its close: project roots are unavailable\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tsource, err := resolver.Roots.StoreFor(identity.Project)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn false, scope + \" of \" + identity.Project + \" cannot be checked for its close: \" + projectResolutionState(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsource = resolver.withSpecSnapshot(identity.Project, source)\n\t\tsource.closeoutChain = s.closeoutChain\n\t\towner = source\n\t}\n\tif owner.FederatedResolver == nil {\n\t\towner.FederatedProjectID, owner.FederatedResolver = identity.Project, &resolver\n\t}\n\tadopted, err := owner.closeoutReviewPolicyAdopted()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false, scope + \" cannot be checked for its close: \" + err.Error()\n\t}\n\tif !adopted || owner.localScopeClosed(scope) {\n\t\treturn true, \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn false, scope + \" is reached but not closed: `pose close \" + scope + \"` publishes its closeout receipt\"\n}\n\n// canonicalMember is milestoneMember after transfer redirects: a local member\n// a transfer moved is its canonical destination, local or external. A\n// redirect that cannot be followed reads as external, so no local consumer\n// judges the redirect stub and federated proof fails closed on it (review\n// round 9, N33).\nfunc (s Store) canonicalMember(raw string) (string, bool) {\n\tslug, external, unresolved := s.CloseoutMemberTarget(raw)\n\tif unresolved != \"\" {\n\t\treturn raw, true\n\t}\n\treturn slug, external\n}\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:468:\t\t\tif statusDone && graphValid && !s.indexMaterial && (proven.Kind == \"milestone\" || proven.Kind == \"roadmap\") {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go:946:\t\tmaterial, err := BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn(Store{\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go:962:\t\tmaterial, err := BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn(store)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go:975:\tmaterial, err := BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn(store)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go:63:\t// indexMaterial marks the store computing an index's federated input\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go:67:\tindexMaterial bool\npose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:323:// AggregateDependencyClosed reports whether a resolved dependency on a\npose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:331:func (s Store) AggregateDependencyClosed(resolver ArtifactResolver, localProject string, resolved ArtifactResolution) (bool, string) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:336:\tif identity.Kind != \"milestone\" && identity.Kind != \"roadmap\" || s.indexMaterial {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/readiness.go:190:\t\t\t} else if closed, why := s.AggregateDependencyClosed(resolver, project, resolved); !closed {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_federated_material.go:53:// BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn returns the specs, roadmaps, semantic