{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'func .*PinIndexes|func .*ReadIndex' pose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go; sed -n '382,426p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go; rg -n 'func .*StoreFor|governanceStores' pose-mcp/internal/pose/roots.go\"","aggregated_output":"356:func (s Store) ReadIndexGeneration() IndexGenerationView {\n406:func (s Store) ReadIndex(name string) ([]byte, IndexGenerationStatus, error) {\n702:func (s Store) PinIndexes() Store {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfiles[f.Name] = data\n\t\t\tif legacy, legacyErr := s.fsys().ReadFile(filepath.Join(indexDir(s.Root), f.Name)); legacyErr != nil || sha256Prefixed(legacy) != f.SHA256 {\n\t\t\t\tdiverged = append(diverged, f.Name)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tagain, againRaw, _, againErr := readIndexDescriptor(s.fsys(), s.Root)\n\t\tif againErr == nil && again.GenerationID == desc.GenerationID && string(againRaw) == string(raw) {\n\t\t\tif problem != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn IndexGenerationView{Status: IndexGenerationUnavailable, Reason: problem, Descriptor: desc}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn IndexGenerationView{Status: IndexGenerationCurrent, Descriptor: desc, Files: files, Diverged: diverged, DescriptorBytes: raw}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn IndexGenerationView{Status: IndexGenerationUnavailable, Reason: \"the generation descriptor kept changing while it was read\"}\n}\n\n// ReadIndex returns the bytes of one index and what may be concluded from them.\n// For a published set the file is checked against the descriptor, so a file that\n// belongs to another generation is an error that wraps ErrIndexGenerationUnavailable.\n// For a repository that never published a set the file is returned as before,\n// with status IndexGenerationLegacy and no claim of coherence. A missing file is\n// os.ErrNotExist in both cases.\nfunc (s Store) ReadIndex(name string) ([]byte, IndexGenerationStatus, error) {\n\tknown := false\n\tfor _, n := range IndexGenerationFiles {\n\t\tknown = known || n == name\n\t}\n\tif !known {\n\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %s is not an index of a generation\", name)\n\t}\n\tif pin := s.indexPin; pin != nil {\n\t\tswitch pin.Status {\n\t\tcase IndexGenerationCurrent:\n\t\t\traw := pin.Files[name]\n\t\t\ts.governanceIndexConsumed(IndexGenerationCurrent, nil, pin)\n\t\t\treturn raw, IndexGenerationCurrent, nil\n\t\tcase IndexGenerationUnavailable:\n\t\t\treturn nil, IndexGenerationUnavailable, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %w: %s\", ErrIndexGenerationUnavailable, pin.Reason)\n\t\t}\n\t\t// A pin taken while the repository had no descriptor does not keep the\n\t\t// bytes: if a first publication has started since, the files may mix two\n\t\t// runs, and the operation is told so instead of reading them.\n\t\tif indexPendingIn(s.fsys(), s.Root) || indexDescriptorExists(s.fsys(), s.Root) {\n63:\t// governanceStores is an operation-local overlay used when a multi-root\n65:\tgovernanceStores map[string]Store\n154:func (r *Roots) StoreFor(projectID string) (Store, error) {\n156:\tguarded, hasGuarded := r.governanceStores[projectID]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defects found in the reviewed scope. Targeted tests and race-enabled regression tests passed. The exact-range artifact check passed with 952 non-blocking provenance warnings; surface-check passed with no findings.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, and delivery-evidence rules. Broader validation relies on sealed evidence. The harne8 reproduction was not independently repeated. The worktree remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the marker's containment and both guarded acceptance paths. Independently reran targeted tests and their race-enabled variants. The harne8 execution log remains implementer evidence, not an independently repeated reproduction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The marker is set on a value copy of Store, introducing no shared mutable synchronization state. Traced checkIndexInputs and the removed local closeout reentry. Targeted race-enabled tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No exported signatures, serialized fields, CLI arguments or MCP schemas changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-input-binding-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolver authorization, identity validation, graph validation, source status and bounded error paths remain in place.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-roadmap-acceptance-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced material construction through roadmap acceptance and source resolution. External source proof and ordinary closeout acceptance retain their existing gates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing actionable resolver errors and closeout blockers remain available outside material computation; no sensitive logging was added.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined Store and acceptance changes. The private marker changes only material computation; without policy adoption the formerly conditional local closeout blocker was already absent. Public contracts remain compatible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The material path skips local terminal projection, while the ordinary path still rejects an unclosed predecessor. Independently executed the new regression, RoundSix and material tests successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-31ba3d16591d2b0e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 removes the circular dependency rather than making input verification reentrant. BuildIndexFederatedMaterialIn marks its Store copy; federatedAcceptance and AggregateDependencyClosed suppress terminal projection only in that context, implementing R1 while preserving R2. No individual structural fact IDs were listed in the brief.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-31ba3d16591d2b0e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the spec's requirements, D1, validation strategy and residual-risk statement with runtime behavior and the permanent validation-matrix command. No public operational contract requires a scaffold migration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ordinary closeout still reports closeout-not-terminal and retains explicit close remediation. Material computation avoids asking the local terminal projection responsible for the documented self-wait.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is supported by the guarded implementation and receipt-read regression; R2 by ordinary acceptance and RoundSix. R3 is supported by removing the documented reentry path and the spec's before/after execution log. The independent targeted and race runs passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-31ba3d16591d2b0e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the complete requested diff, artifact declarations and start record. Implementation is confined to the material marker, its two consumers, regression coverage and validation registration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-roadmap-negative-gates\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed authorization, canonical identity, path confinement, graph validity, source verification and external proof boundaries. The marker is private and cannot be supplied through public input; ordinary authority gates remain enforced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-31ba3d16591d2b0e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A private per-computation flag with two guards is a small cohesive correction. D1's reentrant-check alternative would replace the hang with unknown material. No new cache, framework or public mode was introduced. This choice must be revisited if another local material path begins reading index-derived terminal state.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout --from 5e14337100be40d52508587fbc42a070c0b79c6e --to ee960dffb9ba49a8ad255a31076cf3ca146fef92 --strict --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed against the exact reviewed range with pipeline failure propagation. Exit 0; six claims, 952 warning findings, no error or critical findings. The initial default-range invocation selected additional recorded history and was interrupted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-31ba3d16591d2b0e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed structural evidence and independently inspected the design; did not rerun the assessment in this read-only review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not refresh assessment artifacts. Reviewed the mapped component and sealed validation evidence directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No public inter-module contract changed. Inspected consumers and federation boundaries and used sealed integration evidence without refreshing assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected changed files and the existing debt report; no new TODO, FIXME or panic marker was introduced. Did not write a refreshed assessment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the review conclusion to be recorded and verified first; this task explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion check must follow POSE's recording of this independent review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied the selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-material-does-not-ask-closeout-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout --strict. Exit 0; one delivery target, 216 results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposed from the sealed strict-validation producer run and inspected its recorded results. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation pipeline during this read-only review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed module validation results. Additionally reran targeted regression and material tests, then the regression tests with -race; both independent runs passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
